Noise-injection & obfuscation of door-opening patterns
What you have

Isolation Forest flags every “dip” as an anomaly.

In stream_processor.py you inject large noise (±0.1 °C) whenever a dip occurs, and small noise (±0.02 °C) otherwise.

The subscriber only ever sees the fuzzed values, so the door-opening spikes vanish but the rest of the trace remains visible.

✅ Objective met: identifiable thermal patterns are hidden, while normal readings still flow for “operational” use.

Potential enhancements

Tune your noise magnitude via experiments so that HVAC algorithms (or your PID simulator) still hit set-points within tolerance.

Consider interpolation or splines over multi‐second windows instead of pure random noise for even smoother masking.

